IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja3-sch5-fifth-schedule`

-- scja3-tests-sch5.l4: tests for the Fifth Schedule.  Expected values are written from the text of the Schedule
-- (SCJA1969.txt lines 5956-6170) beside each assertion, and not from the module's output.

§ `Tests: the Fifth Schedule`

GIVEN court IS A Court
      jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction exercised`
      about IS A `Subject of an order or application`
      way IS A `Way an order went`
      agreedFinal IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Decision
`sch 5 test: a decision` MEANS
    Decision WITH
        `made by` IS court
        `in the exercise of` IS jurisdiction
        `nature of the proceeding` IS `a civil proceeding`
        `subject of the case` IS `any other civil matter`
        `the order` IS (Order OF about, way)
        `made after the trial of an action` IS FALSE
        `made by consent of the parties` IS FALSE
        `amount in dispute or value of the subject matter, excluding interest and costs` IS NOTHING
        `date made` IS Date 1 7 2024
        `date the judgment or order was extracted` IS NOTHING
        `a written law provides that it is final or that no appeal lies` IS FALSE
        `the parties agreed in writing, signed by or for each, that it is final` IS agreedFinal

-- positional: judge, payer, limitation, nameCap, newCause, costsOnly, chambers, summary, notDispute, interlocutory, pofmaHearing, pofmaRefused
`sch 5 test: no facts about the order` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: a Judge, and the appellant is the paying party` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: a Judge, limitation expired, name corrected` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: a Judge, limitation expired, new cause of action` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: a Judge, limitation expired, nothing else` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: a Judge, new cause of action, limitation not expired` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: only issue is costs` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: Judge in chambers, summary way, facts not in dispute` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: Judge in chambers, summary way, facts in dispute` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: Judge in open court, summary way, facts not in dispute` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: a Judge at an interlocutory application` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: interlocutory application, no Judge` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: Judge at a POFMA appeal refused to set aside` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`sch 5 test: Judge at a POFMA appeal set the direction aside` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the order` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- positional: s23, originalUnderLaw, allegesFraud, allegesNaturalJustice, agreementPartOnly, appealIsAgainstThatPart
`sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the jurisdiction and finality` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the jurisdiction and finality` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: original jurisdiction under a written law requiring it` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the jurisdiction and finality` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: alleges fraud` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the jurisdiction and finality` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: alleges natural justice breach` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the jurisdiction and finality` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: alleges fraud, agreement covers part only, appeal is against another part` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the jurisdiction and finality` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`sch 5 test: alleges fraud, agreement covers part only, appeal is against that part` MEANS `sch 5 facts about the jurisdiction and finality` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

`sch 5 test: GD unconditional permission to defend` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `permission to defend proceedings` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD conditional permission to defend` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `permission to defend proceedings` `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD set aside a default judgment unconditionally` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `setting aside a default judgment` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD set aside a default judgment on condition` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `setting aside a default judgment` `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD refused to strike out an action` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `striking out an action or a matter commenced by originating process` refused FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD refused to strike out a pleading` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `striking out a pleading or part of a pleading` refused FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD struck out an action` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `striking out an action or a matter commenced by originating process` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD decided an interpleader summons` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `an interpleader summons` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD refused permission to amend` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `amending a pleading` refused FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD gave permission to amend` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `amending a pleading` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD gave security for costs` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `security for costs` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD refused security for costs` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `security for costs` refused FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD gave discovery` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `discovery or inspection of documents` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD refused discovery` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `discovery or inspection of documents` refused FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD refused a stay` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a stay of proceedings` refused FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD gave a stay` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a stay of proceedings` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD order about further evidence` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `adducing further evidence` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD order about summary judgment` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `summary judgment` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD dismissed an action on striking out a pleading` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `dismissing an action, or entering judgment, upon striking out or amendment of a pleading` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD order about costs for hearing dates` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `costs or fees for hearing dates` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` FALSE
`sch 5 test: GD agreed final` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `another order or application` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE
`sch 5 test: SICC agreed final` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `Singapore International Commercial Court` `original jurisdiction` `another order or application` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE
`sch 5 test: DC unconditional permission to defend` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `District Court` `original jurisdiction` `permission to defend proceedings` `granted unconditionally` FALSE
`sch 5 test: DC agreed final` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `District Court` `original jurisdiction` `another order or application` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE
`sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `Family Division of the High Court` `appellate jurisdiction` `another order or application` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` FALSE
`sch 5 test: FD appellate decision agreed final` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `Family Division of the High Court` `appellate jurisdiction` `another order or application` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE
`sch 5 test: FD original decision` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `Family Division of the High Court` `original jurisdiction` `another order or application` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` FALSE
`sch 5 test: FD original decision, unconditional permission to defend` MEANS `sch 5 test: a decision` `Family Division of the High Court` `original jurisdiction` `permission to defend proceedings` `granted unconditionally` FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 1: the appellate court is the court of s 29C ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 1 the appellate court` (JUST `Appellate Division`)) EQUALS JUST `Appellate Division`
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 1 the appellate court` (JUST `Court of Appeal`)) EQUALS JUST `Court of Appeal`
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 1 the appellate court` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 2(2): permission is not required ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(2)(a) permission is not required: a decision of the General Division in its original jurisdiction under a written law requiring that` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: original jurisdiction under a written law requiring it`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the written-law requirement is not met
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(2)(a) permission is not required: a decision of the General Division in its original jurisdiction under a written law requiring that` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- appellate, not original, jurisdiction
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(2)(a) permission is not required: a decision of the General Division in its original jurisdiction under a written law requiring that` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: original jurisdiction under a written law requiring it`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a decision of the District Court is not "a decision of the General Division"
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(2)(a) permission is not required: a decision of the General Division in its original jurisdiction under a written law requiring that` `sch 5 test: DC agreed final` `sch 5 test: original jurisdiction under a written law requiring it`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(2)(b) permission is not required: a decision of the Family Division of the High Court in its original jurisdiction` `sch 5 test: FD original decision`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(2)(b) permission is not required: a decision of the Family Division of the High Court in its original jurisdiction` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(2)(b) permission is not required: a decision of the Family Division of the High Court in its original jurisdiction` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 4(2) ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 4(2) s 29A(1)(b), and s 29A(1)(c) read with para 3, do not apply to the decision` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a Family Division appellate decision that is not under s 23: para 4(2) is silent
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 4(2) s 29A(1)(b), and s 29A(1)(c) read with para 3, do not apply to the decision` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 4(2) s 29A(1)(b), and s 29A(1)(c) read with para 3, do not apply to the decision` `sch 5 test: FD original decision` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 4(2) s 29A(1)(b), and s 29A(1)(c) read with para 3, do not apply to the decision` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- seam 5: an exception takes the case out of s 29A(1)(b) ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 an exception in the Fifth Schedule takes the case out of s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 an exception in the Fifth Schedule takes the case out of s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: original jurisdiction under a written law requiring it`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 an exception in the Fifth Schedule takes the case out of s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: FD original decision` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no exception applies to an ordinary General Division decision
#ASSERT (`sch 5 an exception in the Fifth Schedule takes the case out of s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a District Court decision is outside the Schedule
#ASSERT (`sch 5 an exception in the Fifth Schedule takes the case out of s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: DC agreed final` `sch 5 test: original jurisdiction under a written law requiring it`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 2(1): permission is required in a case within s 29A(1)(b) ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(1) permission of the appellate court is required in a case mentioned in s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the amount exceeds the sum: not a case mentioned in s 29A(1)(b)
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(1) permission of the appellate court is required in a case mentioned in s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an unvalued case: the Act does not say
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(1) permission of the appellate court is required in a case mentioned in s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- para 2(2)(a) and para 4(2) take the case out, whatever the amount
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(1) permission of the appellate court is required in a case mentioned in s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: original jurisdiction under a written law requiring it` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(1) permission of the appellate court is required in a case mentioned in s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(1) permission of the appellate court is required in a case mentioned in s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: FD original decision` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a District Court decision: the paragraph speaks of the General Division
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 2(1) permission of the appellate court is required in a case mentioned in s 29A(1)(b)` `sch 5 test: DC agreed final` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 3 limbs ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(a) a Judge gives unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: GD unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(a) a Judge gives unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: GD unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: no facts about the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(a) a Judge gives unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: GD conditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(b) a Judge gives permission to defend on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 5 test: GD conditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(b) a Judge gives permission to defend on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 5 test: GD conditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge, and the appellant is the paying party`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(b) a Judge gives permission to defend on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 5 test: GD unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(c) a Judge sets aside a default judgment unconditionally` `sch 5 test: GD set aside a default judgment unconditionally` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(c) a Judge sets aside a default judgment unconditionally` `sch 5 test: GD set aside a default judgment on condition` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(d) a Judge sets aside a default judgment on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 5 test: GD set aside a default judgment on condition` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(d) a Judge sets aside a default judgment on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 5 test: GD set aside a default judgment on condition` `sch 5 test: a Judge, and the appellant is the paying party`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(e) a Judge refuses to strike out an action, a matter or a pleading` `sch 5 test: GD refused to strike out an action` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(e) a Judge refuses to strike out an action, a matter or a pleading` `sch 5 test: GD refused to strike out a pleading` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an order striking out is not an order refusing to strike out
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(e) a Judge refuses to strike out an action, a matter or a pleading` `sch 5 test: GD struck out an action` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(f) the only issue in the appeal relates to costs or fees for hearing dates` `sch 5 test: only issue is costs`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(f) the only issue in the appeal relates to costs or fees for hearing dates` `sch 5 test: no facts about the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(g) a Judge in chambers decides an interpleader summons in a summary way, the facts not being in dispute` `sch 5 test: GD decided an interpleader summons` `sch 5 test: Judge in chambers, summary way, facts not in dispute`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(g) a Judge in chambers decides an interpleader summons in a summary way, the facts not being in dispute` `sch 5 test: GD decided an interpleader summons` `sch 5 test: Judge in chambers, summary way, facts in dispute`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(g) a Judge in chambers decides an interpleader summons in a summary way, the facts not being in dispute` `sch 5 test: GD decided an interpleader summons` `sch 5 test: Judge in open court, summary way, facts not in dispute`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(g) a Judge in chambers decides an interpleader summons in a summary way, the facts not being in dispute` `sch 5 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 5 test: Judge in chambers, summary way, facts not in dispute`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(h) a Judge refuses permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD refused permission to amend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(h) a Judge refuses permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD refused permission to amend` `sch 5 test: a Judge, limitation expired, name corrected`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(h) a Judge refuses permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD refused permission to amend` `sch 5 test: a Judge, limitation expired, new cause of action`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(h) a Judge refuses permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD refused permission to amend` `sch 5 test: a Judge, limitation expired, nothing else`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(h) a Judge refuses permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD refused permission to amend` `sch 5 test: a Judge, new cause of action, limitation not expired`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- giving permission to amend is not "refusing" it
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(h) a Judge refuses permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(i) a Judge gives security for costs` `sch 5 test: GD gave security for costs` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(i) a Judge gives security for costs` `sch 5 test: GD refused security for costs` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(j) a Judge gives or refuses discovery or inspection of documents` `sch 5 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(j) a Judge gives or refuses discovery or inspection of documents` `sch 5 test: GD refused discovery` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(j) a Judge gives or refuses discovery or inspection of documents` `sch 5 test: GD gave security for costs` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(k) a Judge refuses a stay of proceedings` `sch 5 test: GD refused a stay` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(k) a Judge refuses a stay of proceedings` `sch 5 test: GD gave a stay` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (l): an interlocutory application other than the ten
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(l) a Judge makes an order at the hearing of an interlocutory application other than for the ten matters` `sch 5 test: GD order about further evidence` `sch 5 test: a Judge at an interlocutory application`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(l) a Judge makes an order at the hearing of an interlocutory application other than for the ten matters` `sch 5 test: GD order about summary judgment` `sch 5 test: a Judge at an interlocutory application`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(l) a Judge makes an order at the hearing of an interlocutory application other than for the ten matters` `sch 5 test: GD gave a stay` `sch 5 test: a Judge at an interlocutory application`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(l) a Judge makes an order at the hearing of an interlocutory application other than for the ten matters` `sch 5 test: GD order about further evidence` `sch 5 test: interlocutory application, no Judge`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(l) a Judge makes an order at the hearing of an interlocutory application other than for the ten matters` `sch 5 test: GD order about further evidence` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the ten matters, one by one
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `summary judgment`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `setting aside a default judgment`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `striking out an action or a matter commenced by originating process`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `striking out a pleading or part of a pleading`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `dismissing an action or a matter commenced by originating process`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `further and better particulars`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `amending a pleading`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `security for costs`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `discovery or inspection of documents`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` interrogatories
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `a stay of proceedings`
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `adducing further evidence`)
-- the core's "dismissing an action upon striking out of a pleading" is not one of the ten as the text lists them (fork)
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 5 para 3(l) the application is for one of the ten matters (i) to (x)` `dismissing an action, or entering judgment, upon striking out or amendment of a pleading`)
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(m) a Judge at the hearing of a POFMA appeal refuses to set aside the direction` `sch 5 test: Judge at a POFMA appeal refused to set aside`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(m) a Judge at the hearing of a POFMA appeal refuses to set aside the direction` `sch 5 test: Judge at a POFMA appeal set the direction aside`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(m) a Judge at the hearing of a POFMA appeal refuses to set aside the direction` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 3 as a whole ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3 permission of the appellate court is required in one of the cases (a) to (m)` `sch 5 test: GD unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3 permission of the appellate court is required in one of the cases (a) to (m)` `sch 5 test: GD refused discovery` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the Singapore International Commercial Court is read as within "General Division" (s 18C)
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3 permission of the appellate court is required in one of the cases (a) to (m)` `sch 5 test: SICC agreed final` `sch 5 test: only issue is costs` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a General Division decision none of the thirteen limbs lists
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3 permission of the appellate court is required in one of the cases (a) to (m)` `sch 5 test: GD struck out an action` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Subject to paragraph 4(2)": a Family Division s 23 decision is out of paragraph 3
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3 permission of the appellate court is required in one of the cases (a) to (m)` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: only issue is costs` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the District Court and a Family Division original decision are outside "a decision of the General Division"
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3 permission of the appellate court is required in one of the cases (a) to (m)` `sch 5 test: DC unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3 permission of the appellate court is required in one of the cases (a) to (m)` `sch 5 test: FD original decision, unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 4(1) ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 4(1) permission of the appellate court is required to appeal a Family Division appellate decision` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 4(1) permission of the appellate court is required to appeal a Family Division appellate decision` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 4(1) permission of the appellate court is required to appeal a Family Division appellate decision` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 5(2) ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the agreement counts whenever it was made` `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) before the decision was made`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the agreement counts whenever it was made` `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) after the decision was made`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the agreement counts whenever it was made` `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) at the same time as the decision`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud, agreement covers part only, appeal is against that part`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud, agreement covers part only, appeal is against another part`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 5(1) ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: alleges natural justice breach`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "(including the Family Division of the High Court)"
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision agreed final` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: SICC agreed final` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no allegation: the second limb is missing
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no agreement in writing: the first limb is missing
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: GD refused discovery` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the agreement covers part only, and the appeal is against another part
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud, agreement covers part only, appeal is against another part`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud, agreement covers part only, appeal is against that part`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 5(1) permission of the appellate court is required where the parties agreed in writing the decision is final and the appellant alleges fraud, illegality or a breach of natural justice` `sch 5 test: DC agreed final` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- seam 6: a case specified in para 3, 4(1) or 5(1), no exception applying ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the case is one specified in paragraph 3, 4(1) or 5(1) of the Fifth Schedule and no exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD refused discovery` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the case is one specified in paragraph 3, 4(1) or 5(1) of the Fifth Schedule and no exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD agreed final` `sch 5 test: no facts about the order` `sch 5 test: alleges fraud`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a Family Division s 23 decision: paragraph 4(1) holds even though paragraph 4(2) takes it out of paragraph 3
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the case is one specified in paragraph 3, 4(1) or 5(1) of the Fifth Schedule and no exception applies` `sch 5 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 5 test: only issue is costs` `sch 5 test: section 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an ordinary General Division decision that no paragraph lists
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the case is one specified in paragraph 3, 4(1) or 5(1) of the Fifth Schedule and no exception applies` `sch 5 test: GD struck out an action` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a District Court decision: outside the Schedule
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the case is one specified in paragraph 3, 4(1) or 5(1) of the Fifth Schedule and no exception applies` `sch 5 test: DC unconditional permission to defend` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- seam 7: the court from which permission must be obtained ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the court from which permission must be obtained` `sch 5 test: GD refused discovery` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` (JUST `Appellate Division`) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST `Appellate Division`
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the court from which permission must be obtained` `sch 5 test: GD refused discovery` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` (JUST `Court of Appeal`) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST `Court of Appeal`
-- via para 2(1): an amount within s 29A(1)(b)
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the court from which permission must be obtained` `sch 5 test: GD struck out an action` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` (JUST `Appellate Division`) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST `Appellate Division`
-- permission is not required under the Schedule: it names no court
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the court from which permission must be obtained` `sch 5 test: GD struck out an action` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` (JUST `Appellate Division`) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the court of s 29C is not known: NOTHING passes through
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the court from which permission must be obtained` `sch 5 test: GD refused discovery` `sch 5 test: a Judge made the order` `sch 5 test: no jurisdiction or finality facts` NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- the helpers ----
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 5 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 the order gave` `granted unconditionally`
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 5 the order gave` refused)
#ASSERT `sch 5 the order gave or refused` refused
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 5 the order gave or refused` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal`)
